    {
      "id": 35420,
      "nameEs": "Code_18",
      "originalName": "Code_18",
      "year": 2011,
      "igdbId": 18072,
      "popularity": 0,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "best_version",
          "value": "86175",
          "source": "script",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Code_18",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Code_18",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Code_18 is the fifth entry in the Infinity series, which also includes Never 7: The End of Infinity, Ever 17: The Out of Infinity, Remember 11: The Age of Infinity, and 12Riven: The Psi-Climinal of Integral. The game follows Hayato Hino, a high school student who receives voice messages from the future on his phone, and is stuck in a loop, repeating a month of his life over and over again.\n\nCyberfront bought the rights to the Infinity series after its previous developer, KID, closed down. The game's writing was done by the group Run & Gun, while the sound production was handled by the band Milktub. While the development team had originally planned to use a theme of \"escape from an enclosed space\" similarly to previous Infinity games, it was changed due to concerns of the size of the game's audience, and was seen as a reboot of the series.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Code_18 es la quinta entrega de la serie Infinity, que también incluye Never 7: The End of Infinity, Ever 17: The Out of Infinity, Remember 11: The Age of Infinity y 12Riven: The Psi-Climinal of Integral. El juego sigue a Hayato Hino, un estudiante de secundaria que recibe mensajes de voz desde el futuro en su teléfono y queda atrapado en un bucle, repitiendo un mes de su vida una y otra vez.\n\nCyberfront compró los derechos de la serie Infinity después de que su desarrollador anterior, KID, cerrara. La escritura del juego corrió a cargo del grupo Run & Gun, mientras que la producción de sonido estuvo a cargo de la banda Milktub. Aunque el equipo de desarrollo había planeado originalmente usar el tema de \"escape de un espacio cerrado\", similar a los juegos anteriores de Infinity, se cambió por preocupaciones sobre el tamaño de la audiencia del juego, y se consideró un reinicio de la serie.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "2011",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
